21:   // hook is executed. It is important that we can set and return this
22:   // variable synchronously, because every time we `throw` for Suspense, this
23:   // hook will unmount and a new instance will be created, destroying whatever
24:   // state existed. Thus, if this hook were to try to always set and return
25:   // `stateSession`, it would cause an infinite loop:
26:   //   1. instance A mounts
27:   //   2. instance A receives value, calls `setStateSession`
28:   //   3. instance A throws
29:   //   4. instance A unmounts
30:   //   5. instance B mounts
31:   //   ...
